Backport of open upstream PR sgl-project/sglang#29927 ("[SM120]
DeepSeek-V4: DeepGEMM paged-MQA indexer + FP4 MoE + page-split") to
v0.5.16, pinned 2026-08-06. Code-level pieces: batched sparse-MLA prefill
(query rows > 64 route to flashinfer's _sparse_mla_sm120_paged_attention
instead of the head-padded decode kernel), indexer metadata chunked at
M=4096 for DeepGEMM's shared-memory cap, u64-lane page-split, a
dynamic-smem budget probe in the metadata kernel, Triton hc_combine, and
HC-prenorm token-count dispatch. The env-path recipe on top of this
(DeepGEMM fp8_paged_mqa_logits indexer + HC prenorm, the +19-25% prefill
numbers in the README) additionally requires sgl-deep-gemm 0.1.5.post1 --
see the Dockerfile.

DEVIATION vs upstream, deliberate: the >64-row batched-prefill route is
gated on topk == 512. Ungated, DSPARK draft/verify batches (indexer
topk=192, in no CUTLASS bucket) get routed into the sparse-MLA prefill
kernel, which crashes, and the server crash-loops at boot warmup.
Upstream cannot observe this: main cannot boot DSPARK on SM120 at all
without #33407 (this repo's dspark-sm120-decode-dispatch.diff), so #29927
and #33407 need each other for spec-decode-on SM120. topk=512 batches
(the real prefill/verify shapes the PR targets) take the new route;
topk=192 keeps the #33407 decode dispatch.

Backport surgery vs the PR diff: kernels/jit/csrc -> jit_kernel/csrc
(v0.5.16 predates upstream's kernel-tree restructuring); import-context
re-anchors in mhc.py / indexer.py / metadata.py / deepseek_v4.py (v0.5.16
lacks main's dsa_topk_backend branch); attn_tp_size -> tp_size in
deepseek_v4.py (pre-DP-rename). Test hunks stripped.

